yNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-04-14T12:01:31Z","updated_at":"2025-04-14T12:14:59Z","closed_at":"2025-04-14T12:14:07Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105381","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105381","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105381.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105381.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Add Vector2.reversed() and Vector3.reversed() methods\r\nSummary: This PR introduces two new methods, Vector2.reversed() and Vector3.reversed(), that allow easy reversal of vector components. These methods multiply the x, y, and z components of the vectors by -1, effectively flipping the direction of the vector.\r\n\r\nWhy this is useful: These methods simplify vector manipulation when you need to reverse a vector quickly. This can be useful in various situations, such as inverting directions, or for physics and game mechanics where vectors may need to be flipped.\r\n\r\nUsage Example in GDScript:\r\n\r\nvar vec2 = Vector2(8, 9)\r\nvec2.reversed()\r\nprint(vec2)  # Output: (-8, -9)\r\nThis PR aims to enhance the utility of Vector2 and Vector3 classes with a simple yet effective method to reverse vector components.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105381/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105381/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}